"Don't use a hard line limit, use TypeScript best practices"

In TypeScript, a module is a file that does one job and declares what it imports and exports. Cutting at a line count splits one piece of logic across files and tangles the imports.

"Assemble, never reimplement" (library use)
What is a library dependency?
